I am playing in a world with entities that can be provinces and planets, there is a global condition called harmony, some entities can be in pain, and an entity can crave another entity.
Here are the actions I can do: Attack an entity; Succumb an entity; Overcome an entity with respect to another entity; Feast an entity upon another entity.
I can only attack an entity X if X is a province, X is a planet, and harmony currently holds. When I attack X, X becomes in pain, X stops being a province, X stops being a planet, and harmony no longer holds.
I can only succumb an entity X if X is in pain. When I succumb X, X becomes a province, X becomes a planet, harmony holds, and X is no longer in pain.
I can only overcome an entity X with respect to another entity Y if Y is a province and X is in pain. When I overcome X with respect to Y, harmony holds, X becomes a province, X comes to crave Y, Y stops being a province, and X is no longer in pain.
I can only feast an entity X upon another entity Y if X craves Y, X is a province, and harmony holds. When I feast X upon Y, X becomes in pain, Y becomes a province, X no longer craves Y, X stops being a province, and harmony no longer holds.
